# Windsurf Rules — Forge Project

## Language & runtime

- Go 1.24+, module `github.com/teragrid/forge`
- CGO_ENABLED=0 — no C imports
- Target: linux/amd64, linux/arm64, darwin/amd64, darwin/arm64, windows/amd64

## Repository layout

```
cmd/forge/          main entry point
internal/cli/       one cmd<verb>/ package per verb
internal/           shared packages
docs/               specs, ADRs, task lists
tests/fixtures/     test data
```

## Mandatory patterns

### New verb checklist
- [ ] `internal/cli/cmd<verb>/<verb>.go` — `package cmd<verb>`
- [ ] `New() *cobra.Command` exported
- [ ] `verbmeta.Register(...)` in `init()`
- [ ] Error codes registered (unique range from `docs/ERROR_CODES.md`)
- [ ] Added to `internal/cli/root.go` AddCommand + import

### Security rules (non-negotiable)
- User paths → `internal/fssandbox` before any file I/O
- Subprocesses → `internal/procspawn` allow-list
- LLM calls → `internal/llmprovider` only
- No `os.Exit` outside main.go
- No PII in logs or telemetry

## Build verification

```bash
go build ./...   # zero output required
go vet ./...     # zero output required
go test ./...    # all pass
```

## Documentation

- ADRs live in `docs/adr/` — add one for significant design decisions
- RFCs live in `docs/rfcs/` — required for breaking changes or new protocols
- Task progress tracked in `docs/tasks/DEVELOPMENT_TASKS.md`
